  "details": {
    "$comment": "The public detail fields, for the listings named. `rows` is each listing's database state as getListingDetail reads it (`fork.parent` names the listing its fork pointer holds, by slug). `stream` is the detail part of the store-listing@v1 body the adapter publishes from it to the read model (the service audience). `expected` is the detail an anonymous viewer is served: the same on both sides, `connectClientId` (off-site only) is the detail's `kindData.connectClientId`, and `forkOf` is per viewer (the parent named only when that viewer is shown the parent, by the store's gate; `name` is the parent's name, which in this fixture is its slug). The site side runs `rows` through projectListingDetail, resolveForkAttribution and the adapter (listingExtrasFromRow, listingBody); the read model runs `stream` through its ingest and ProjectDetail.",
